# Environment/secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# application.properties is intentionally COMMITTED.
# It contains development defaults only - every real credential is read from an
# environment variable (see .env.example). This is the 12-factor approach: config
# that differs per environment lives in the environment, not in the repository.
#
# If you ever place a real secret in it, add a local override file instead:
#   src/main/resources/application-local.properties  (git-ignored)

